Negative control for the TWO named error presets (`R6-19`).

Conflates them again: `error-action` stops aiming at the write and fails the
READ instead, exactly as the single `error` preset did — so picking "row action
refused" empties the collection, the rows the operator was looking at vanish,
and the state on screen is the OTHER preset's. `error-collection` and the
recorded refusal itself are untouched, so what goes red is only the ruled
distinction: the two are different states of the surface, and the action error
leaves the list loaded with its rows and refuses one row's write with the API's
own sentence.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the T3.11 preset spec — the action-error case (a GET is served as
recorded, so the collection still answers with its rows).

diff --git a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/force/presets.ts b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/force/presets.ts
--- a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/force/presets.ts
+++ b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/force/presets.ts
@@ -128,8 +128,7 @@
   // body (`R6-19`), so it needs a status and nothing else; the module's own
   // refusal supplies one where the corpus holds it, and `REFUSED` where it does
   // not. No body is authored on either path (`S13`).
-  if (preset === "error-action")
-    return isRead(method) ? served : (failure ?? served);
+  if (preset === "error-action") return withoutBody(failure ?? REFUSED);
 
   if (preset === "error-collection")
     return isRead(method) ? withoutBody(failure ?? REFUSED) : served;
